After 9 years, you would think this company has had more than enough time to make sure the game works before taking it out of early access.
Bought the game on sale, installed, started it up.  It was looking for a file modconfig.xml in the Documents folder which it couldn't find.  Spent hours trying the troubleshooting provided and that didn't work.  Reported the bug.  Thread got deleted.  Commented in someone else's thread that it was a known issue and that i returned the game.  That got deleted as well.  No, I don't recommend a game from a group that actively deletes people reporting an issue with their game.
Edit 10/24/2017:
@all asking for proof of deleted comments/threads: Do you not understand how stupid that sounds?  How can I provide proof for something that is already deleted.  When you get an item or comment deleted in Steam, you get a notification.  When you click that notification, that notification disappears from Steam as it can't take you to the deleted item.
@all asking for the actual issue that is being reported for the bug: Go to discussions, look up "modconfig.xml".  There are several threads on that (unless they are "accidently" deleted before you have the chance to).
@all looking for any reviews of any game: It's always recommended to get your reviews from multiple places to determine whether it's worth putting your money into or not.  I bought this game based on reviews/videos I have seen for this game and the fact that it was on sale.  As stated in the comments below, everyone's mileage is going to vary.
I think this is going to be the last comment/edit I make here as I have already covered everything that I want to say on it and I no longer have this game.  This discussion turned from constructive critism to salty really fast.  For those actually interested in assisting with the problem, you should either send an e-mail to
or post in the Steam discussion per the dev comments below.
